+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static coffee website. Node.js 22.14+ is required for the build and checks; there are no npm dependencies or client-side scripts.
+
+```sh
+npm test
+npm run build
+```
+
+Deploy only `dist/`. Netlify uses `netlify.toml` and the copied `_headers` file. Vercel uses `vercel.json`. For other hosts, configure every response with the headers in `_headers`; copying that file alone does not make an arbitrary HTTP server apply headers. Serve production traffic over HTTPS and redirect HTTP at the hosting edge. HSTS applies to this host only. The previous unpinned `pnpm dlx statikk` start command was removed so serving the site does not download and execute an unaudited package.
+
+The HTML includes a fallback CSP and referrer policy. Frame protection, permissions restrictions, HSTS, cache controls, and MIME sniffing protection require real HTTP response headers. The policy deliberately blocks scripts, network APIs, forms, and frames. Do not relax it to enable injected hosting analytics. The build copies an explicit list of public files, excluding source, configuration, tests, and any local secrets.
+
+## Privacy and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed November 13, 2026. This is a source and configuration review, not an independent certification or a live deployment audit.
+
+| Surface | Finding and handling |
+| --- | --- |
+| Hero photo | Previously requested directly from Unsplash on every visit, exposing visitor connection information to that provider. The same photo is now a local JPEG in `assets/coffee.jpg`; no browser request goes to Unsplash. Source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80 |
+| Fonts and styles | System fonts and local CSS only; no font CDN or external stylesheets. |
+| Client scripts and packages | None. No analytics, advertising, pixels, SDKs, cookies, browser storage, fingerprinting, service workers, telemetry, or CSP reporting endpoints. Script execution and network APIs are blocked by CSP. |
+| Forms and accounts | No data collection or account backend exists. Removed the nonfunctional GET logout link; future logout must use a CSRF-protected state-changing request. Existing menu/account/order links are placeholders for services that are outside this repository. |
+| Hosting | Required to deliver pages and necessarily sees connection metadata. Provider identity, logging, retention, location, access controls, and any injected code cannot be determined from this repository. Header configuration is supplied for Netlify and Vercel, but deployment has not been inspected. |
+
+`npm test` checks the reviewed pages and CSS for third-party resources, inline execution, and collection surfaces; checks both hosting header configurations for consistency; and builds the site to verify that only reviewed assets are deployed. These are regression guards for this static implementation, not a general HTML/CSS security parser. Review new files and any dependency or hosting change before adding it to the public build.
+
+## Secure handling for future features
+
+Keep browsing anonymous. Before adding an account, order form, or external service, record each required field, purpose, provider, retention period, and deletion mechanism. Collect only the information needed for the requested service. Keep optional marketing separate and disabled until chosen; update the privacy page before collection. Audit a vendor's requested access, transmitted fields, retention, subprocessors, and deletion support before integration; repeat when scope changes. Prefer local assets and remove unused vendors.
+
+Process personal information on a dedicated HTTPS backend. Validate and limit inputs there, encode outputs for their context, and use parameterized database operations. Keep credentials, tokens, and personal data out of HTML, URLs, browser storage, analytics, and logs. Use secure, HttpOnly, SameSite session cookies, CSRF protection for state changes, least-privilege access, and defined retention/deletion rules. Set `Cache-Control: no-store` on personalized responses and do not place them in shared caches. This repository has no backend implementing those future services.
+
+At deployment, disable host-injected analytics and minimize access logs: omit query strings and referrers, redact identifiers, restrict operator access, and define the shortest operational retention needed. Identify the actual hosting provider and its retention/access practices in the privacy notice once selected. Never promise that the host collects no data. Reapply the header configuration on migrations and error responses. Do not add cookies or consent controls when there is nothing optional to consent to.
+
+Policy references: [MDN CSP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP), [frame-ancestors HTTP requirement](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/frame-ancestors), [referrer policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Practical_implementation_guides/Referrer_policy).
